luci-app-apmond (2.0.0beta)
  * Change - Access points: easier to read; ULA as a short LuCI link with the address as tooltip, IPv4 without the prefix length, uptime in two units [bluewavenet]
  * Change - Access points: one radio table per node, a row per AP with band, channel, mode, power, SSID and interface, VLAN and VXLAN columns only when used [bluewavenet]
  * Change - Access points and Clients: client columns that are empty for every client are left out, Wi-Fi signal and TX / RX bitrates as "-43 dBm" and "6.0 / 390.0 Mbit/s" [bluewavenet]
  * Change - Access points: each node's radios and clients are indented under its row on a light theme background [bluewavenet]
  * Fix - wired clients: the port speed is shown as "Link 100 Mbit/s", not as TX/RX bitrate (Access points and Clients) [bluewavenet]
  * Fix - Status: the default passphrase notice points to Settings instead of /etc/config/apmond [bluewavenet]
  * Change - for apmond 2.x: every page reads the apmond ubus object through rpcd (rpc.declare) instead of running the apmond script; needs apmond 2.0 or later [bluewavenet]
  * Change - ACL: ubus apmond status, nodes, node, clients (read) and forget (write), uci apmond, and only /usr/sbin/apmond read_log as a command [bluewavenet]
  * Add - common.js with the ubus calls, formatting and the version footer (luci-app-apmond and apmond package version with build commit), replaces version.js [bluewavenet]
  * Add - Status: grouped tables, warnings for restart needed, clock not synced and a rejected last report [bluewavenet]
  * Add - Access points: state ok/late/lost with report age, apmond package version with restart needed, radios with SSID and VLAN per AP, VXLAN and last seen per client, late/lost nodes and stale clients greyed out, Forget for lost nodes and stale clients, nodes on the default passphrase listed [bluewavenet]
  * Add - Clients page: every client of every node in one list with a filter, Forget for stale clients [bluewavenet]
  * Add - Log: Follow button, re-reads the log every 10 seconds [bluewavenet]
  * Fix - Makefile: no .js.o files are left in the package when jsmin is missing [bluewavenet]
  * Change - Settings: the apmond 2.x options (role, port, collector, interface, netdev, key_epoch, prev_epoch_grace, client_stale_timeout, max_message_size), 1.x only options removed, passphrase as a password field; Save & Apply restarts apmond through its reload trigger [bluewavenet]

